um of colors, each corresponding to a specific wavelength of light. When this sunlight enters Earth’s atmosphere, it interacts with the gases that make up the air, such as nitrogen and oxygen. These gas molecules are significantly smaller than the wavelengths of visible light, which is the critical condition for Rayleigh scattering to occur.\n\nRayleigh scattering"}